0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, APRIL 19, 2006\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman (arrived at 8:15 p.m.), Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Lysik, Parker, Peirce, Steller, Tamuri.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Michael Hafken.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\rCouncilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Washburn presented Employee Service Awards to Tina Wallace for five years of service and Jeff Rubin for ten years of service. Mayor Washburn presented a special recognition to Michael Hafken for his exceptional work on the marketing campaign for the secondhand smoke ordinance. Mayor Washburn also presented a proclamation to June Aiello in honor of the Boys & Girls Clubs of Conejo & Las Virgenes and to Samantha Spencer, the Youth of the Year. Mayor Washburn introduced Kesha Dorsey, Calabasas High School student, who participated in the Future Foundation Youth Congress. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian announced that the Calabasas Fine Arts Festival will be held on May 6 and 7, 2006.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT: \r\r Sue Somber, Calabasas, Barbara Wilson, Calabasas and J. Housman, Calabasas, expressed concern over a neighbor who installed an un-permitted swimming pool, as well as bright lights and loud speakers, that create a nuisance to the neighborhood. Michael Raich, Calabasas, and David Yee, Calabasas, spoke regarding poor road conditions in the Mulholland Heights neighborhood and expressed concern that the Sheriff�s Department does not patrol that area.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of the minutes for the April 5, 2006 City Council meeting. \r\r Recommendation to approve a renewal of the animal control services agreement with the County of Los Angeles. \r \r Request for the City to quitclaim 1,507 square feet of real property known as Pansy Trail located in the Calabasas Highlands. \r\r Recommendation to approve guidelines for authorizing Sheriff enforcement in private communities. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1016, authorizing enforcement of Section 21107.7 of the California Vehicle Code to specific roads within the Oaks of Calabasas (Tract 35596). \r\r Recommendation to approve a professional services agreement with W.R. Lind, Incorporated, to perform professional surveying services. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1018, supporting efforts to protect Proposition 42 funding. \r\r Recommendation to approve a street name change for a portion of an interior access road for the Shea Homes development (TM 53534, CUP 99-05, SPR 99-03 and OAK 00-04) located at 4700 Las Virgenes Canyon Road. \r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1019, in support of AB 2015, which enhances municipal membership on the South Coast Air Quality Management District (SCAQMD). \r\r Approval of replacing an hourly Accounting Specialist in the Finance Department with a full-time Accounting Specialist. \r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to approve Items #1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10 with Item #5 being CONTINUED to May 3, 2006. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rSPECIAL ITEM \r\r Report from the Executive Director of the Council of Governments. \r\rNo Action Taken.\r\r Report from Spirit of Calabasas regarding Hurricane Katrina relief efforts. \r\rNo Action Taken. \r\rThe following item was heard out of order of the agenda.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING \r\r CONTINUED PUBLIC HEARING - Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1012, approving a mitigated negative declaration; adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1013, approving GPA-004-003, PM-004-001, CUP-004-006, VAR-004-005 and OTP-005-009; and motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2006-223, approving ZCH-004-005 for the subdivision of one parcel into two parcels, rough grading of one pad and driveway on one resulting parcel, and development of one single-family home including a pool/spa, horse stable/corral area, septic system, driveway, and retaining walls and dedication of 8.7 acres of permanent open space on the second resulting property located at 24135 Mulholland Highway (APN�s: 4455-006-012, -013). \r \rCouncilmember Wolfson and Councilmember Groveman recused themselves due to the proximity of their residences to the project and left the room. \r\rMayor Washburn opened the public hearing.\r\rGlenn Michitsch, Planner and Tom Bartlett, City Planner, provided the staff report.\r\rSteve Harris, Mountains Restoration Trust, provided information on the trail and open space designation associated with the project. Rob Searcy, Architect, and Andy Howard, Applicant, provided background information on the proposed project.\r\rMayor Washburn closed the public hearing.\r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to adopt Resolution 2006-1012, approving a mitigated negative declaration; adopt Resolution No. 2006-1013, approving GPA-004-003, PM-004-001, CUP-004-006, VAR-004-005 and OTP-005-009; and motion to waive further reading and introduction of Ordinance No. 2006-223. MOTION CARRIED 3/0 with Councilmember Wolfson�s and Councilmember Groveman�s recusal.\r\r\r\r\r\rNEW BUSINESS\r\rDiscussion of code related issues regarding equestrian uses on upper Las Virgenes Road. \r\rMayor pro Tem Bozajian recused himself due to the proximity of his residence to the subject area and left the room.\r\rTom Bartlett, City Planner, provided the staff report.\r\r Stephanie Abronson, Monte Nido, Don Wallace, Las Virgenes Homeowners Federation and Cold Creek Community Council, spoke in support of the zoning for equestrian properties in the City to allow 8 horses per acre. Melanie Beck, representing the National Park Service, spoke regarding a trailhead that is planned abutting the subject property and spoke in support of the trail riding business being legally permitted. Frances Alet, Calabasas, spoke in support of each equestrian property being reviewed on an individual basis rather than amending the City�s zoning code and spoke in support of the conditional use permit being approved for the applicant at the Farmhouse property. Nolan Burkholder, Calabasas, read a letter from Mary Hubbard, which spoke in opposition to a zoning code or general plan amendment for equestrian uses.\r\r The City Council provided direction to staff on possible alternatives.\r\rThe City Council recessed at 10:05 p.m. and reconvened at 10:20 p.m.\r\r Adoption Of Resolution 2006-1020, approving partial transfer of solid waste annual hauler permit from Consolidated Disposal Service, dba Las Virgenes Disposal to Waste Management, dba GI Industries. \r\rAlex Farassati, Environmental Services Manager, provided the staff report.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson to adopt Resolution 2006-1020, approving partial transfer of solid waste annual hauler permit from Consolidated Disposal Service, dba Las Virgenes Disposal to Waste Management, dba GI Industries. MOTION CARRIED 4/0. Councilmember Groveman abstained.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2006-1017, in support of Measure G, the Las Virgenes Unified School District�s general obligation bond measure on the June 6, 2006 State General Election ballot. \r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Maurer to adopt Resolution 2006-1017, in support of Measure G, the Las Virgenes Unified School District�s general obligation bond measure on the June 6, 2006 State General Election ballot. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of March 30, 2006 to April 7, 2006. \r\r No Action Taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Maurer reported on the Headwaters Task Force meeting. Mayor Washburn stated that the bids for the Civic Center project will be opened on May 9.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles stated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\rThe City Council requested the status of the beautification of Mulholland Highway.\r\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 11:20 p.m. \r\r\r\r\r____________________________________ \rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 4 -\u0015\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r04/19/06\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0